00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:43.780
And the way to the higher testing numbers
most likely is going to be an antigen test.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:50.130
An important element to understand right now,
Corona virus tests are PCR tests.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:54.530
That's typically a favorite test because of
its accuracy.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.669
But it takes a lot of resources, material
resources and personnel resources.

00:05:58.669 --> 00:06:02.180
It's very hard to scale PCR testing to the
numbers we need.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:07.250
The PCR test works by looking for evidence
of the genetic material of the virus in the

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.350
body.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:12.470
Now you have a different type of test that
can be developed called an antigen test.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.099
This is what we have for the flu right now.

00:06:15.099 --> 00:06:20.710
And the antigen test looks for what are called
the viral surface proteins.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.639
Antigen testing is much simpler.

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:25.150
You can scale it way more dramatically.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.450
The tough part is developing the antigen test.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:33.050
To start with, you need a deeper understanding
of the virus which proteins to look for.

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:37.770
Once you figure out how to make an antigen
test, you can develop many more tests.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:43.180
One million a day, two million a day would
be practical really with an antigen test.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:47.710
Then even Dr. Burke's admitted a couple weeks
ago, you're not going to test the country

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.880
of 300 million with a PCR test, which is what
we have now.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:53.370
We need an antigen test.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:07:10.590
